// Test: error.interface-typed-function-type-return
typealias Integer = int(i64.min to i64.max)

interface Shape
	function area() returns Integer
end 'Shape'

typealias MakeFn = function(Integer) returns Shape

function apply(f MakeFn) returns Integer
	return f(1).area()
end 'apply'

function main() returns ExitCode
	return 0 as ExitCode
end 'main'
---
CompilerError:
error E2015: <fragment>:8:38: Unsupported: a function's return type declared at the interface type 'Shape' — a value held at an interface type is a two-word fat pointer `(value, witness)`, and a return hands back one register, plus a second only for a throwing call's error flag — an interface-returning ABI is a distinct slice. Declare it at a concrete type, or take the interface as a PARAMETER of a plain function, which carries its witness as an adjacent argument
